@prefix ldh:    <https://w3id.org/atomgraph/linkeddatahub#> .
@prefix rdf:    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix dh:     <https://www.w3.org/ns/ldt/document-hierarchy#> .
@prefix dct:    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<> a dh:Item ;
    dct:title "Add data" ;
    dct:description "Copy RDF data from Linked Data resources and file uploads into your dataspace" ;
    rdf:_1 <#content> .

<#content> a ldh:XHTML ;
    rdf:value """<div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
    <p class="lead">Copy RDF data from Linked Data resources and file uploads into your dataspace</p>
    <p>Forking copies the contents of any RDF document into a named graph in your dataspace. Two sources of RDF are supported: RDF resources on the web (Linked Data) and RDF file uploads.</p>
    <div class="alert alert-info">
        <p>Adding data this way will cause a blocking request, so use it for small amounts of data only (e.g. a few thousand RDF triples).
        For larger data, use asynchronous <a href="../import-data/import-rdf-data/" target="_blank">RDF imports</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ldhc-tabs or-horizontal">
        <div class="ldhc-tablist sz-md va-line" role="tablist">
            <button aria-controls="from-linked-data-pane" aria-selected="true" class="ldhc-tab is-on" id="from-linked-data-tab" role="tab" type="button"><span class="ldhc-tab-lbl">From Linked Data</span></button>
            <button aria-controls="from-the-command-line-pane" aria-selected="false" class="ldhc-tab" id="from-the-command-line-tab" role="tab" type="button"><span class="ldhc-tab-lbl">From the command line</span></button>
            <button aria-controls="from-a-file-pane" aria-selected="false" class="ldhc-tab" id="from-a-file-tab" role="tab" type="button"><span class="ldhc-tab-lbl">From a file</span></button>
        </div>
        <div aria-labelledby="from-linked-data-tab" class="ldhc-tabpanel" id="from-linked-data-pane" role="tabpanel">
        <div class="screenshot-placeholder">
            <span class="msi" aria-hidden="true">play_circle</span>
            <p>Screen recording: forking a remote RDF document into the dataspace</p>
        </div>
        <p>To copy the contents of the current RDF document (local or remote) into a local document, follow these steps:</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Click on the <span class="btn btn-save-as">Save</span> button on the right side of the <a href="../../reference/user-interface/#action-bar" target="_blank">action bar</a>.
                A form will open with the following fields:
                <dl>
                    <dt>Source</dt>
                    <dd>URI of the source document</dd>
                    <dt>Graph</dt>
                    <dd>The target document. The source data is appended to the target document's existing content, replacing nothing. You can start typing to find the document by its label, or paste its URI here.</dd>
                </dl>
            </li>
            <li>Click <span class="btn btn-primary btn-save">Save</span> to perform the fork operation.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>For example, the Northwind Beverages category <a href="../../reference/imports/rdf/">maps to</a> the UNESCO Thesaurus concept
            <a href="https://unesco-thesaurus.demo.linkeddatahub.com/concepts/concept3683/" target="_blank"><samp>Beverages</samp></a>. Open it in the
            <a href="../browse-data/">Linked Data browser</a> and fork it into your own dataspace.</p>
        <p>The target document does not have to be local: you can also add data to a document in <em>another</em> dataspace by pasting its URI. The
            append is performed with your identity, so the target dataspace's <a href="../../reference/administration/acl/">access control</a> decides
            whether it is allowed — a refusal surfaces as a form error.</p>
        </div>
        <div aria-labelledby="from-the-command-line-tab" class="ldhc-tabpanel" hidden="hidden" id="from-the-command-line-pane" role="tabpanel">
        <p>The same fork is a pipe — <samp>ldh get</samp> the source, <samp>ldh post</samp> it into the target document:</p>
        <pre>ldh get --accept text/turtle \\
    "https://unesco-thesaurus.demo.linkeddatahub.com/concepts/concept3683/" \\
  | ldh post -t text/turtle "${LDH_BASE}categories/1/"</pre>
        </div>
        <div aria-labelledby="from-a-file-tab" class="ldhc-tabpanel" hidden="hidden" id="from-a-file-pane" role="tabpanel">
        <p>To upload the contents of an RDF file into a document, drag the file from your filesystem into LinkedDataHub when the document's <a href="../../reference/user-interface/#layout-modes">properties mode</a> is active.</p>
        <p>The following syntaxes are supported:</p>
        <table class="table table-striped">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Syntax</th>
                    <th>File extensions</th>
                    <th>Media type</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>N-Triples</td>
                    <td><samp>.nt</samp></td>
                    <td><samp>application/n-triples</samp></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Turtle</td>
                    <td><samp>.ttl</samp></td>
                    <td><samp>text/turtle</samp></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>RDF/XML</td>
                    <td><samp>.rdf</samp>, <samp>.owl</samp></td>
                    <td><samp>application/rdf+xml</samp></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>JSON-LD</td>
                    <td><samp>.jsonld</samp></td>
                    <td><samp>application/ld+json</samp></td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="lead"><a href="../browse-data/">Browse data</a> to find resources worth forking, or <a href="../import-data/import-rdf-data/">import RDF data</a> for larger datasets.</p>
</div>"""^^rdf:XMLLiteral .
